Revision history for Perl extension Proc::FastSpawn

1.2.2  Thu Oct  8 00:00:00 UTC 2026
	- a "dir" option: the directory the child runs in, honoured by all
	  four. A relative program path is resolved against it here, in the
	  parent, so that changing directory in the child (posix) and
	  lpCurrentDirectory (win32, which resolves the program against the
	  parent's directory) mean the same thing. Where the directory can
	  only be changed by the child, a bad one is exit 126 rather than a
	  failed spawn, 127 being a failed exec.

1.2.1  Tue Aug  4 00:00:00 UTC 2026
	- add spawn3/spawn3p: spawn with stdin/stdout/stderr redirection.
	  A descriptor that is already its own target is left alone, so they
          are a superset of spawn/spawnp.
	- spawn3/spawn3p return a Proc::FastSpawn::Child rather than a bare
	  pid. It behaves as a pid and carries the process handle an event
          loop needs on win32.
	- win32: spawn/spawnp go through CreateProcess rather than the _spawn
	  family, which offered no way to reach the creation flags.
	- win32: from vista on, the child is given only the handles it was
	  meant to get, rather than every inheritable handle in the process.
	- an optional trailing option hash. inherit => 0 holds the child to
	  0, 1 and 2, which otherwise needed fd_inherit on every descriptor
	  in turn.
	- setOptions sets the process-wide CreateProcess defaults, so a
	  program can ask for CREATE_NO_WINDOW once at startup instead of
	  having it imposed. The defaults are what the _spawn family passed.

1.2  Mon Jun 10 05:02:10 CEST 2013
        - do not use vfork with spawnp, to avoid running into lots of
          problems (execvp might call malloc, better thread safety etc.),
          at the cost of using fork instead of vfork.
        - fix a (rather theoretical) memory corruption bug.

1.1  Sun Apr 28 02:47:31 CEST 2013
	- add spawnp function for convenience.

1.0  Sun Apr  7 03:32:54 CEST 2013
	- work around corrupted $^X on openbsd, when linked against
          libpthread (only affects a testcase).

0.2  Thu Apr  4 08:24:32 CEST 2013
        - define _WIN32_WINNT to windows xp, to make sure
          we get the GetProcessId prototype.
	- add synopsis section with some examples.

0.1   Sat Mar 30 02:16:48 CET 2013
	- intiial CPAN release.

0.01  Fri Mar 29 14:32:28 CET 2013
	- first rough idea.

